# Range D: F_0d4bc .. F_10960  (render modules: intro, front end screens, fonts, fades,
# board/creature sprite drawing, level select). Each render module has a Load (called
# from Render_LoadAll), an Init (Render_InitAll) and a Free (Render_FreeAll) entry.
# Shared helpers used here (named by other ranges): F_13844 = logic (back) screen,
# F_13830 = physic (shown) screen, F_1385c = background screen, F_1376a = swap screens,
# F_162da = clear a screen, F_1636a = copy a 32000-byte screen, F_007a2 = relocate a
# .BSB sprite block, F_0aac0 = "machine has less than 2 MB" (low-memory mode),
# F_10e0c/F_10e30 = low-memory asset cache pages. B_2db20 is the shared GodLib
# graphic canvas (VRAM ptr at +0, draw functions at +$c, clipped functions at +$10;
# function +$18 = DrawSprite, +$c = DrawBox).

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ arrows (tail)
# F_0d4bc is already named ArrowGfx_DrawSprite in C.map (arrows module); kept commented here
# to avoid a duplicate entry. Suggested header if C.map lacks one:
# F_0d4bc ArrowGfx_DrawSprite
# @ArrowGfx_DrawSprite ArrowGfx_DrawSprite(d0 = frame, d1 = x, d2 = y, a0 = screen): draws frame d0
# @ArrowGfx_DrawSprite of the ARROWS.BSB sprite block (B_2beba) at pixel (x,y) on the given screen,
# @ArrowGfx_DrawSprite through the shared canvas's DrawSprite function.

