# ------------------------------------------------------------------ congratulations screen
F_0d9e0 Congrats_Load
@Congrats_Load Congrats_Load(): loads and relocates CONGRATS.BSB unless the machine is in
@Congrats_Load low-memory mode (then Congrats_ReloadLowMem fetches it from the asset cache);
@Congrats_Load resets the message type to 0.
F_0da0e Congrats_InitFireworks
@Congrats_InitFireworks Congrats_InitFireworks(): resets the 8 firework records (gFireworks,
@Congrats_InitFireworks $204 bytes each) and staggers their start delays (3 frames apart).
F_0da48 Congrats_Free
@Congrats_Free Congrats_Free(): frees CONGRATS.BSB (only when it was loaded, i.e. not in
@Congrats_Free low-memory mode).
F_0da60 Congrats_Run
@Congrats_Run Congrats_Run(): the "congratulations" screen after a completed set: selects asset
@Congrats_Run page 0, plays music 12, fades to the board palette, then each frame draws the
@Congrats_Run fireworks, the CONGRATS sprite and one or two message sprites (gCongratsType; two
@Congrats_Run in gGameMode 1) until fire or key $44 (F10) is pressed.
F_0dbc6 Congrats_SetType
@Congrats_SetType Congrats_SetType(d0 = type): chooses which message the congratulations
@Congrats_SetType screen shows (stored in gCongratsType).
F_0dbce Congrats_DrawFireworks
@Congrats_DrawFireworks Congrats_DrawFireworks(): updates and draws the fireworks on the back
@Congrats_DrawFireworks screen (F_157f0 does the work).
F_0dbdc Congrats_ResetFirework
@Congrats_ResetFirework Congrats_ResetFirework(a0 = firework): restarts one firework: random
@Congrats_ResetFirework delay 4-7, random x 10-309, y = 198, upward speed -5 or -6.
F_0dc32 Congrats_ReloadLowMem
@Congrats_ReloadLowMem Congrats_ReloadLowMem(): low-memory mode only: takes CONGRATS.BSB from
@Congrats_ReloadLowMem asset cache page 0 (entry 0) and relocates it.
B_2befa gCongratsSprite
B_2befe gCongratsType
B_2bf00 gFireworks

